WEBVTT

00:00:07.384 --> 00:00:09.734
Let me introduce you
to your new

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:13.477
Defense Against the Dark Arts
teacher...

00:00:13.477 --> 00:00:14.609
me.

00:00:15.827 --> 00:00:18.395
Gilderoy Lockhart.

00:00:18.395 --> 00:00:21.355
Order of Merlin, Third Class.

00:00:21.355 --> 00:00:23.313
Honorary member

00:00:23.313 --> 00:00:25.794
of the Dark Force
Defense League

00:00:25.794 --> 00:00:28.275
and five times winner...

00:00:28.275 --> 00:00:30.668
of Witch Weekly's

00:00:30.668 --> 00:00:34.803
Most-Charming-Smile Award.

00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:36.413
But I don't talk about that.

00:00:36.413 --> 00:00:38.372
I didn't get rid
of the Bandon Banshee

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:39.590
by smiling at him.

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:45.901
Now...

00:00:45.901 --> 00:00:47.772
be warned.

00:00:47.772 --> 00:00:49.905
It is my job to arm you

00:00:49.905 --> 00:00:53.822
against the foulest creatures
known to wizardkind.

00:00:55.737 --> 00:00:58.000
You may find yourselves

00:00:58.000 --> 00:00:59.959
facing your worst fears
in this room.

00:00:59.959 --> 00:01:04.093
Know only that no harm
can befall you whilst I am here.

00:01:04.093 --> 00:01:07.705
I must ask you not to scream.

00:01:07.705 --> 00:01:09.098
It might provoke them!

00:01:09.098 --> 00:01:13.015
[SQUEALING]

00:01:13.015 --> 00:01:15.409
Cornish pixies?

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:18.499
Freshly caught
Cornish pixies.

00:01:18.499 --> 00:01:21.154
Laugh if you will,
Mr. Finnegan,

00:01:21.154 --> 00:01:22.677
but pixies can be

00:01:22.677 --> 00:01:25.549
devilishly tricky
little blighters.

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.334
Let's see what you make of them.

00:01:27.334 --> 00:01:28.813
Hyah! Go!

00:01:31.816 --> 00:01:33.514
Come on, now.

00:01:33.514 --> 00:01:36.908
Round them up, round them up!
They're only pixies!

00:01:53.664 --> 00:01:56.015
Please, get me down!

00:01:58.104 --> 00:01:59.540
Get off me!

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.324
Stop. Hold still.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:05.024
Peskipiksi Pesternomi!

00:02:10.638 --> 00:02:13.032
Yeeeeehah!

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:26.654
I'll ask you three

00:02:26.654 --> 00:02:30.005
to just nip the rest of them
back into their cage.

00:02:31.441 --> 00:02:33.661
What do we do now?

00:02:35.184 --> 00:02:36.838
Immobulus!

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.068
Why is it always me?

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:55.900
I spent the summer

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:57.815
devising a whole new
Quidditch program.

00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:01.341
We're going to train earlier,
harder and longer.

00:03:01.341 --> 00:03:02.907
What--?

00:03:02.907 --> 00:03:04.996
I don't believe it!

00:03:07.434 --> 00:03:09.088
Where do you think
you're going, Flint?

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.524
Quidditch practice.

00:03:10.524 --> 00:03:12.482
I booked the pitch
for Gryffindor today.

00:03:12.482 --> 00:03:13.875
Easy, Wood.

00:03:13.875 --> 00:03:15.833
I've got a note.

00:03:15.833 --> 00:03:19.054
Uh-oh, I smell trouble.

00:03:19.054 --> 00:03:20.621
"I, Professor Severus Snape,

00:03:20.621 --> 00:03:22.797
"do hereby give
the Slytherin team

00:03:22.797 --> 00:03:24.581
"permission
to practice today,

00:03:24.581 --> 00:03:26.453
owing to the need
to train their new Seeker."

00:03:26.453 --> 00:03:28.150
You've got a new Seeker? Who?

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.287
Malfoy?

00:03:34.287 --> 00:03:35.810
That's right.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:37.725
And that's not all
that's new this year.

00:03:38.856 --> 00:03:41.642
Those are Nimbus 2001s.

00:03:41.642 --> 00:03:43.339
How did you get those?

00:03:43.339 --> 00:03:44.862
A gift from Draco's father.

00:03:44.862 --> 00:03:46.908
You see, Weasley,
unlike some,

00:03:46.908 --> 00:03:49.302
my father can afford the best.

00:03:49.302 --> 00:03:51.086
At least no one
on the Gryffindor team

00:03:51.086 --> 00:03:52.392
had to buy their way in.

00:03:52.392 --> 00:03:54.307
They got in on pure talent.

00:03:58.398 --> 00:04:00.878
No one asked
your opinion.

00:04:00.878 --> 00:04:02.576
You filthy little Mudblood.

00:04:04.055 --> 00:04:07.233
You'll pay for
that one, Malfoy.

00:04:07.233 --> 00:04:09.148
Eat slugs!

00:04:15.850 --> 00:04:18.374
You okay, Ron?

00:04:20.724 --> 00:04:23.162
Say something.

00:04:24.772 --> 00:04:27.992
CHILDREN:
Ew. Yuck!

00:04:29.037 --> 00:04:31.039
Wow! Can you
turn him around, Harry?

00:04:31.039 --> 00:04:34.085
No, Colin.
Get out of the way.

00:04:34.085 --> 00:04:36.523
Let's take him
to Hagrid's.

00:04:36.523 --> 00:04:39.308
He'll know what to do.

00:04:47.055 --> 00:04:50.145
This calls for
a specialist's equipment.

00:04:53.931 --> 00:04:55.803
Nothing to do
but wait till it stops,

00:04:55.803 --> 00:04:57.065
I'm afraid.

00:04:59.981 --> 00:05:01.983
Better out than in.

00:05:01.983 --> 00:05:04.203
Who was Ron trying to curse,
anyway?

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.074
Malfoy.

00:05:06.074 --> 00:05:08.468
He called Hermione...

00:05:08.468 --> 00:05:11.340
Well, I don't know
exactly what it means.

00:05:16.084 --> 00:05:18.042
He called me a Mudblood.

00:05:18.042 --> 00:05:20.480
He did not.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.829
What's a Mudblood?

00:05:21.829 --> 00:05:23.831
It means dirty blood.

00:05:23.831 --> 00:05:26.921
Mudblood's a really foul name
for someone who is Muggle-born.

00:05:26.921 --> 00:05:31.360
Someone with non-magic parents.
Someone like me.

00:05:31.360 --> 00:05:34.233
It's not a term
one usually hears

00:05:34.233 --> 00:05:36.191
in civilized conversation.

00:05:36.191 --> 00:05:38.367
See, the thing is, Harry,

00:05:38.367 --> 00:05:41.414
there's some wizards,
like the Malfoy family,

00:05:41.414 --> 00:05:43.633
who think they're better
than everyone else,

00:05:43.633 --> 00:05:45.679
because they're what people call
pure-blood.

00:05:45.679 --> 00:05:48.508
That's horrible!

00:05:51.293 --> 00:05:52.729
It's disgusting.

00:05:52.729 --> 00:05:56.124
And it's codswallop, to boot.
Dirty blood...

00:05:56.124 --> 00:05:58.169
Why, there isn't a wizard
alive today

00:05:58.169 --> 00:05:59.954
that's not half-blood or less.

00:05:59.954 --> 00:06:01.738
More to the point,

00:06:01.738 --> 00:06:03.958
they've yet to think of a spell
that our Hermione can't do.

00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:05.873
Come here.

00:06:08.528 --> 00:06:10.617
Don't you think on it, Hermione.

00:06:10.617 --> 00:06:14.621
Don't you think on it
for one minute.

00:06:14.621 --> 00:06:16.449
Hey?

00:06:22.193 --> 00:06:25.414
Harry, Harry, Harry...

00:06:25.414 --> 00:06:27.851
Can you possibly imagine

00:06:27.851 --> 00:06:31.246
a better way
to serve detention

00:06:31.246 --> 00:06:34.554
than by helping me
to answer my fan mail?

00:06:34.554 --> 00:06:36.033
Not really.

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:38.949
Fame is a fickle friend,
Harry.

00:06:38.949 --> 00:06:42.431
Celebrity is as celebrity does.

00:06:42.431 --> 00:06:45.129
Remember that.

00:06:48.829 --> 00:06:51.788
Come....

00:06:53.616 --> 00:06:56.532
Come to me.

00:06:57.794 --> 00:06:59.709
Come to me.

00:06:59.709 --> 00:07:01.276
What?

00:07:01.276 --> 00:07:02.886
Sorry?

00:07:04.192 --> 00:07:05.976
That voice.

00:07:07.151 --> 00:07:08.805
Voice?

00:07:11.895 --> 00:07:13.680
Didn't you hear it?

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:17.988
What are you talking about,
Harry?

00:07:17.988 --> 00:07:21.122
I think you're getting
a bit...drowsy,

00:07:21.122 --> 00:07:23.429
and, great Scott, no wonder.
Look at the time.

00:07:23.429 --> 00:07:25.561
We've been here
nearly four hours.

00:07:25.561 --> 00:07:30.479
Spooky how the time flies
when one's having fun.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.659
Spooky.

00:07:40.141 --> 00:07:42.361
Blood.

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:46.060
I smell blood.

00:07:46.060 --> 00:07:49.324
Let me rip you.

00:07:49.324 --> 00:07:54.111
Let me kill you.

00:07:54.111 --> 00:07:57.071
Kill.

00:07:57.071 --> 00:07:58.115
Kill!

00:07:58.115 --> 00:08:00.161
Kill!

00:08:00.161 --> 00:08:01.162
Harry...

00:08:01.162 --> 00:08:02.381
Did you
hear it?

00:08:02.381 --> 00:08:03.512
Hear what?

00:08:03.512 --> 00:08:04.905
That voice.

00:08:04.905 --> 00:08:07.429
Voice? What voice?

00:08:07.429 --> 00:08:09.300
I heard it first
in Lockhart's office,

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.085
and then again just--

00:08:11.085 --> 00:08:14.001
It's time.

00:08:14.001 --> 00:08:15.698
It's moving.

00:08:15.698 --> 00:08:16.873
I think it's going to kill.

00:08:16.873 --> 00:08:19.528
Kill?

00:08:19.528 --> 00:08:21.748
Harry, wait!
Not so fast!

